# Testing & quality

- **Testing frameworks + ≥ 80% coverage:** see `testing-standards.mdc` and `test-coverage.mdc`.
  Tests live under `tests/` mirroring `src/`; cross-app E2E goes in a Playwright
  suite when present.
- Test the **public surface** of a module, not its internals.
- **Descriptive file names.** One production file per resource; helper/util only
  after 1000 code lines — see `file-colocation.mdc`. The 1000-line cap does not
  apply to files under `tests/`.
- **No deep cross-module imports** — modules expose a public surface (`index.js`).
- **Document every function** with JSDoc (purpose, params, returns). Other comments explain
  **why / intent**, not a line-by-line narration of what the code does.
- A change is **done** only when tests pass, lint is clean (when wired), and the
  relevant docs/ADRs are updated.
- **Never commit secrets.** Document env vars in `.env.example`.
- Record any new architectural decision as an ADR in `docs/adr/`.

See root `AGENTS.md` and `docs/` when present.
